<title>GERMANY: Colonia 1996 net profit rises 12 pct.</title>
<headline>Colonia 1996 net profit rises 12 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			236	vs 210</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		  444	up around 10 pct</p>
<p>    Dividend (Common stock)	     34 pct   vs 28 pct</p>
<p>    Dividend (Preferred stock)	  36 pct   vs 30 pct</p>
<p>    Earnings per share		    9.75 dmk vs 9.30 dmk</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German insurer is CKAG Colonia Konzern AG. The dividend rise brings the common stock dividend to 1.70 marks per share and the preferred stock dividend to 1.80 marks per share.</p>
<p>In a mandatory statement, Colonia said the profit rise was caused by higher efficiency within its group, a modest rise in costs, continued satisfactory claims development and the good performance of capital investments.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
